They both noticed it at the same time. No jealousy. None. They wanted him happy more than they wanted him exclusive. The realization sat soft between them.
Free Love’s side effect ran that deep. It didn’t just pull. It rewired the part that would have fought over him. That was why Johnny Sinner never noticed his own quirk until the hour he died—women had always acted a certain way around him, and the lack of conflict felt normal. Curtis was the same. He lay there with two girls who should have been measuring each other and instead were just breathing against him, and he didn’t see the quirk at all.
Hina pressed a kiss to his shoulder. Yui’s arm draped across his stomach. Neither of them moved to leave. The unfinished suite stayed quiet around the three of them while the side effect did exactly what it had always done, and Curtis simply thought the stories had been wrong.
